/**
 * @defgroup modulation_without_unload_compressor_assessment Modulation Without Unload
 * @ingroup compressor_modeling
 * @brief Power-law model for a compressor that remains loaded while inlet capacity is modulated.
 * @details
 * The model converts between normalized package power and delivered airflow. Use measured or catalog
 * full-load power and airflow, no-load package power, and the control exponent. Correct the full-load
 * anchors for pressure and inlet conditions first when required. The same curve is also the modulation
 * submodel used above the unload point by modulation-with-unload and variable-displacement controls.
 *
 * @image html ca-modulation-without-unload.svg "Normalized modulation-without-unload curve from the 85.4 kW, 473 acfm test fixture."
 *
 * @heading{Performance Curve and Outputs}
 * @formula{mod-without-unload-power-from-airflow;
 *   P=(P_{FL}-P_{NL})f_Q^m+P_{NL}
 * }
 * @formula{mod-without-unload-airflow-from-power;
 *   Q=Q_{FL}\left(\frac{f_PP_{FL}-P_{NL}}{P_{FL}-P_{NL}}\right)^{1/m}
 * }
 * In the modulation submodel, replace @math{P_{NL}} with
 * @math{P_{max,mod}=f_{P,FL}P_{max}} and replace the upper power anchor with @math{P_{max}}.
 *
 * @heading{Inputs and Origins}
 *
 * | Quantity | Origin | Unit |
 * |---|---|---|
 * | Full-load package power and airflow | measured test or manufacturer package data | kW, acfm |
 * | No-load package power | measured no-load condition or catalog | kW |
 * | Exponent @math{m} | selected control correlation | dimensionless |
 * | Maximum power and modulation floor | load/unload submodel anchors, when used there | kW, fraction |
 *
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{P; Calculated package input power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{Q; Calculated delivered airflow; \acfm}
 * @symrow{P_{FL}; Full-load package power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{Q_{FL}; Full-load airflow; \acfm}
 * @symrow{P_{NL}; No-load package power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{P_{max}; Maximum package power in the modulation submodel; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{P_{max,mod}; Modulation power floor; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{f_{P,FL}; Modulation floor divided by maximum package power; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_P; Full-load package power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_Q; Full-load airflow fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{m; Control-curve exponent; \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * @heading{Fully Substituted Example}
 * The tested fixture uses @math{P_{FL}=85.4\ \mathrm{kW}}, @math{Q_{FL}=473\ \mathrm{acfm}},
 * @math{P_{NL}=55.3\ \mathrm{kW}}, and @math{m=1}. At @math{f_P=0.89},
 * @math{Q=473[(0.89(85.4)-55.3)/(85.4-55.3)]=325.38\ \mathrm{acfm}}. The final result is
 * @math{P=0.89(85.4)=76.01\ \mathrm{kW}} and 325.38 acfm.
 *
 * @heading{Assumptions and Limits}
 * - Inputs below no-load power do not represent a stable point on this loaded modulation curve.
 * - The exponent is an empirical control-shape parameter, not a thermodynamic exponent.
 * - Apply the curve independently to every measured profile interval.
 *
 */
